QuickJS for generated9

Build with the native compiler and APE:

    cd /sys/src/cmd/6c
    mk
    mk test
    mk install
    cd /sys/src/cmd/quickjs
    mk clean
    mk
    mk test
    mk install

The bootstrap 6c predates the NaN comparison fix; rebuild it first.
The build checks that fix, bootstraps qjsc, and compiles the upstream REPL
into qjs. Binaries go to /$objtype/bin.

    qjs -e 'print(2n ** 100n)'
    qjs program.js
    qjs -m module.js
    qjs --std -e 'print(os.platform); print(std.loadFile("/dev/sysname"))'

With no arguments, qjs starts the ANSI REPL. Use a serial terminal or vt
under rio; type \q to exit. The built-in std and os modules provide files,
processes, environment, pipes and timers. os.platform is "plan9".
Use /bin/rc or /bin/ape/sh for an explicit shell; /bin/sh is not assumed.

The example ray tracer writes a binary PPM; width and height are optional
(default 480 by 300). Run page inside rio:

    qjs examples/raytrace.js 800 500 > /tmp/spheres.ppm
    page /tmp/spheres.ppm

qjsc -c emits bytecode as C; -e adds main. Compile with the pcc flags and
OFILES in mkfile, as mk test does. Automatic executable generation is not
configured. Rebuild bytecode when the engine version changes.

Limits

Tested on amd64. Node.js and browser APIs, workers, Atomics and dynamic C
modules are unavailable. The event loop uses APE select, with descriptors
0..95. Writable descriptors are reported ready without checking capacity;
a large pipe write can block. Use small writes or separate processes.

Plan 9/APE provide no symbolic links. stat has second-resolution times and
no blocks property; local timezone conversion uses APE's 32-bit time_t.
Terminal dimensions are unavailable. std.urlGet needs an external curl,
which this port does not supply.

Tests

mk test runs upstream language, closure, loop, BigInt, cyclic-import and
built-in tests, plus native I/O, numeric, process, timer and failure cases.
It also compiles and runs qjsc output.

test_std.js assumes Unix shell paths and links; test_rw_handler.js exceeds
APE's descriptor limit. These and worker/dynamic-module tests are excluded.
Test262 has not been run; full conformance is not claimed.
See doc/quickjs.html for the API and UPSTREAM for sources and licenses.
